## 6. Test Schedule / Milestone
- Test design: 2 days
- Environment setup: 1 day
- Script development: 2 days
- Execution: 2 days
- Reporting: 1 day
**Total duration:** 1 week
**Resources:** 1 QA Automation Engineer, 1 Test Lead

---

## 7. Roles & Responsibilities
- QA Automation Engineer: Script development, execution
- Test Lead: Planning, reporting, risk management

---

## 8. Assumptions
- Jira API endpoint and credentials are available for testing
- Mock/stub services can be configured for negative scenarios
- Test data can be provisioned for all credential states

---

## 9. Risks & Mitigations
| Risk ID | Description | Impact | Likelihood | Mitigation |
|---------|-------------|--------|------------|------------|
| R1 | Dynamic Jira API endpoint or credential rotation | High | Medium | Use environment variables and credential vaults; automate token refresh |
| R2 | Unstable network or proxy failures during API calls | Medium | Medium | Use tcconfig to simulate and test network drops; implement retry logic |
| R3 | Incomplete error propagation for 401 Unauthorized | High | Low | Add regression tests for all error paths; monitor logs for silent failures |
| R4 | Test data provisioning delays (inaccessible issue IDs) | Medium | Medium | Pre-seed test data and use mocks for negative cases |
| R5 | Tool integration/configuration issues (PyTest, Playwright, etc.) | Medium | Low | Validate toolchain in CI pipeline before execution |

